### Justification
The Abortion Legislation Act 2020 contains no provisions outlining a legal duty to provide medical care to a fetus born alive after an abortion. This is confirmed by the [parliamentary record](https://www.parliament.nz/en/pb/hansard-debates/rhr/combined/HansDeb_20190808_20190808_12), which shows that an amendment proposed by Simon O’Connor to explicitly require such medical intervention was [debated and voted down](https://bothlivesmatter.org.nz/the-law-in-detail/) by a margin of 80 to 37. Consequently, the 2020 Act removed the specific duty that had previously existed under the [Contraception, Sterilisation, and Abortion Act 1977](https://bothlivesmatter.org.nz/the-law-in-detail/#About-section7-born-alive).